\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\fi0\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ltrpar{\loch
Formally, we show how to generate a sequence of reward signals, that sequentially optimized give rise\line to a policy with entropy close to optimal. Our main theorem gives a bound on the number of calls to the\line planning oracle, which is independent of the size of the state space of the MDP. Next, we outline the efficient\line construction of such oracles and state the resultant sample & computational complexity in the tabular MDP\line setting. As a proof of concept, we implement our method and show experiments over several mainstream RL\line tasks in Section 5.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
1.1 Informal statement of contributions\line To facilitate exploration in potentially unknown MDPs within a restricted policy class, we assume access to\line the environment using the following two oracles:}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
Approximate planning oracle: Given a reward function (on states) r : S \u8594\'3f R and a sub-optimality\line gap \u949\'3f, the planning oracle returns a stationary policy \u960\'3f = ApproxPlan(r, \u949\'3f) with the guarantee that\line V (\u960\'3f) \u8805\'3f max\u960\'3f V (\u960\'3f)\u8722\'3f \u949\'3f, where V (\u960\'3f) is the value of policy \u960\'3f.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
State distribution estimate oracle: A state distribution oracle estimates the state distribution\line d\u770\'3f\u960\'3f = DensityEst(\u960\'3f, \u949\'3f) of any given (non-stationary) policy \u960\'3f, guaranteeing that \u8214\'3fd\u960\'3f \u8722\'3f d\u770\'3f\u960\'3f\u8214\'3f\u8734\'3f \u8804\'3f \u949\'3f.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
Given access to these two oracles, we describe a method that provably optimizes any continuous and\line smooth objective over the state-visitation frequencies. Of special interest is the maximum entropy and relative\line entropy objectives.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
