\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\fi0\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\ltrpar{\loch
2 Preliminaries\line Markov decision process: An infinite-horizon discounted Markov Decision Process is a tuple M =\line (S,A, r, P, \u947\'3f, d0), where S is the set of states, A is the set of actions, and d0 is the distribution of of the\line initial state s0. At each timestep t, upon observing the state st, the execution of action at triggers an\line observable reward of rt = r(st, at) and a transition to a new state st+1 \u8764\'3f P (\u183\'b7|st, at). The performance on an\line infinite sequence of states & actions (hereafter, referred to as a trajectory) is judged through the (discounted)\line cumulative reward it accumulates, defined as}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
V (\u964\'3f = (s0, a0, s1, a1, . . . )) = (1\u8722\'3f \u947\'3f)\line \u8734\'3f\u8721\'3f\line t=0}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
\u947\'3ftr(st, at).}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
Policies: A policy is a (randomized) mapping from a history, say (s0, a0, r0, s1, a1, r1 . . . st\u8722\'3f1, at\u8722\'3f1, rt\u8722\'3f1),\line to an action at. A stationary policy \u960\'3f is a (randomized) function which maps a state to an action in a\line time-independent manner, i.e. \u960\'3f : S \u8594\'3f \u8710\'3f(A). When a policy \u960\'3f is executed on some MDP M, it produces a\line distribution over infinite-length trajectories \u964\'3f = (s0, a0, s1, a1 . . . ) as specified below.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
P (\u964\'3f |\u960\'3f) = P (s0)\line \u8734\'3f\u8719\'3f\line i=0}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
(\u960\'3f(ai|si)P (si+1|si, ai))}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
The (discounted) value V\u960\'3f of a policy \u960\'3f is the expected cumulative reward an action sequence sampled from\line the policy \u960\'3f gathers.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
