5.1 Environments and the discretization procedure\line The 2-dimensional state spaces for MountainCar and Pendulum (from [BCP+16]) were discretized evenly to\line grids of size 10\u215\'d7 9 and 8\u215\'d7 8, respectively. For Pendulum, the maximum torque and velocity were capped at\line 1.0 and 7.0, respectively.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
The 29-dimensional state space for Ant (with a Mujoco engine) was first reduced to dimension 7, combining\line the agent\u8217\'92s x and y location in the gridspace with a 5-dimensional random projection of the remaining 27\line states. The x and y dimensions were discretized into 16 bins in the range [\u8722\'3f12, 12]. The other dimensions\line were each normalized and discretized into 15 bins in the range [\u8722\'3f1, 1]. While the planning agent agent had\line access to the full state representation, the density estimation was performed exclusively on the reduced\line representation.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
5.2 Algorithmic details\line Reward function. Each planning agent was trained to maximize a KL divergence objective function, ie.\line KL(Unif||d\u960\'3f).}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
MountainCar and Pendulum. The planning oracle is a REINFORCE [SMSM00] agent, where the the\line output policy from the previous iteration is used as the initial policy for the next iteration. The policy class is\line a neural net with a single hidden layer consisting of 128 units. The agent is trained on 400 and 200 episodes\line every epoch for MountainCar and Pendulum, respectively. The baseline agent chooses its action randomly at\line every time step.}
\par \pard\plain \s21\loch\sb0\sa283\ql\sb0\sa283\ltrpar{\loch
Ant. The planning oracle is a Soft Actor-Critic [HZAL18] agent. The policy class is a neural net with 2\line hidden layers composed of 300 units and the ReLU activation function. The agent is trained for 30 episodes,\line each of which consists of a roll-out of 5000 steps. The mixed policy is executed over 10 trials of T = 10000\line steps at the end of each epoch in order to approximate the policy distribution and compute the next reward\line function. The baseline agent chooses its actions randomly for the same number of trials and steps.}
